- id: "R2-N1"
  summary: "Title/framing promises general answer but experiments only cover SFT ≤3B"
  category: framing
  severity: critical
  status: resolved
  first_raised_round: 2
  last_seen_round: 6
  mentions:
    - {round: 2, reviewers: "R1,R2", note: "Table 2: vanilla 2PL MAE ≤ ContamCal on all benchmarks. Title/Abstract promise contamination-aware calibration but experiments show standard IRT suffices."}
    - {round: 3, reviewers: "R1,R2", note: "Title still 'ContamCal'. Abstract implies contamination-specific modeling."}
    - {round: 4, reviewers: "R1,R2", note: "Title 'Decomposing Contamination from Calibration' promises decomposition but core result is nothing to decompose (~0.6-0.7pp). 'Diagnostic value' pivot introduced too late (§1 ¶4). R1 and R2 both AGREE this is narrative mismatch. Suggest empirical investigation framing."}
    - {round: 5, reviewers: "R1,R2", note: "Title changed to question form but framing still inconsistent."}
    - {round: 6, reviewers: "R1,R2", note: "Title question form improved but still over-scopes."}
    - {round: 8, reviewers: "", note: "本轮未提及。D149+ rewrite resolved this issue. Title now 'Not All Models Are Inflated'."}
    - {round: 9, reviewers: "", note: "本轮未提及（fresh review）。Title framing no longer flagged."}
    - {round: 10, reviewers: "", note: "本轮未提及（fresh review）。Title framing resolved."}
  action_items:
    - {round: 2, action: "Reframe paper", assigned_to: "paper_agent", status: "done"}
    - {round: 3, action: "Change title, rewrite Abstract/Contributions", assigned_to: "paper_agent", status: "done"}
    - {round: 4, action: "Reframe as empirical investigation rather than method paper", assigned_to: "paper_agent", status: "done"}
    - {round: 5, action: "Rewrite Introduction from ¶1 as question-driven empirical investigation", assigned_to: "paper_agent", status: "done"}
    - {round: 6, action: "Modify title to scope claim", assigned_to: "paper_agent", status: "done"}
  resolution: "D149+ rewrite: Title changed to 'Not All Models Are Inflated: Profiling Contamination Dose-Response Across Model Families'. Paper repositioned as systematic empirical investigation of dose-response across 5 models (7B-14.7B) from 4 families. No over-scoping."
  resolution_round: 7

- id: "R2-W6"
  summary: "SFT injection ecological validity insufficient — null finding may be SFT artifact, not general property"
  category: experiment
  severity: critical
  status: resolved
  first_raised_round: 2
  last_seen_round: 9
  mentions:
    - {round: 2, reviewers: "R1,R2", note: "Intro motivates with pretraining but experiments only SFT."}
    - {round: 3, reviewers: "R1,R2", note: "Limitations one sentence only."}
    - {round: 4, reviewers: "R1,R2", note: "Elevated to critical. All claims must be scoped to 'under SFT injection at ≤3B scale'."}
    - {round: 5, reviewers: "R1,R2", note: "Claims now scoped with 'Under SFT injection at ≤3B' in Abstract."}
    - {round: 6, reviewers: "R1,R2", note: "Conclusion 'applies directly to settings with larger effects' is unsupported forward claim."}
    - {round: 8, reviewers: "R1,R2", note: "Re-raised as Should-Fix. Both agree SFT ecological validity is known limitation."}
    - {round: 9, reviewers: "R1,R2", note: "Re-raised. Consensus: Limitations discussion still too brief. Expand with Schaeffer et al. comparison."}
    - {round: 10, reviewers: "", note: "本轮未直接提及（fresh review）。Section 6 includes Schaeffer et al. comparison. Limitations includes SFT caveat."}
  action_items:
    - {round: 9, action: "Expand SFT discussion in Section 6 with Schaeffer et al. comparison", assigned_to: "paper_agent", status: "done"}
  resolution: "Section 6 rewritten with Schaeffer et al. comparison. Confounders listed. Limitations includes LoRA SFT caveat."
  resolution_round: 9

- id: "R3-W10"
  summary: "Additive linear γ assumption untested — oracle ablation cannot distinguish null effect from model misspecification"
  category: method
  severity: critical
  status: resolved
  first_raised_round: 3
  last_seen_round: 6
  mentions:
    - {round: 3, reviewers: "R1", note: "Linear γ may average down to non-significant."}
    - {round: 4, reviewers: "R1,R2", note: "Elevated to critical. Oracle ablation has two interpretations."}
    - {round: 5, reviewers: "R1,R2", note: "§5.1 oracle paragraph now presents both interpretations."}
    - {round: 6, reviewers: "R1,R2", note: "Both unanimously re-raise as critical. R2 proposes threshold DGP simulation."}
    - {round: 8, reviewers: "", note: "DGP robustness appendix addresses this."}
    - {round: 9, reviewers: "", note: "本轮未提及（fresh review）。"}
    - {round: 10, reviewers: "", note: "本轮未提及（fresh review）。DGP simulation in Appendix P addresses concern."}
  resolution: "400-run threshold DGP simulation completed. Appendix P written."
  resolution_round: 7

- id: "R4-N1"
  summary: "Domain-level γ significance (Social Sciences 1/8) — P(γ<0) inconsistency and Bonferroni claim unstable"
  category: method
  severity: critical
  status: open
  first_raised_round: 4
  last_seen_round: 10
  mentions:
    - {round: 4, reviewers: "R1,R2", note: "Bonferroni α=0.00625; CI upper bound likely includes zero."}
    - {round: 5, reviewers: "R1,R2", note: "Social Sciences at 99.1% does not pass Bonferroni."}
    - {round: 6, reviewers: "R1,R2", note: "J=16 data available but main text §5.4 still presents J=13."}
    - {round: 9, reviewers: "", note: "本轮未提及（fresh review）。J=16 now in main text."}
    - {round: 10, reviewers: "R1,R2", note: "CONSENSUS Must-Fix. R1-N1 discovers P(γ<0) inconsistency: §5.7 reports 99.7% but Appendix K Table 10 shows 98.48% under same N(0,1) prior (ESS>3800 rules out MCMC noise). Bonferroni threshold 99.375% not met by Table 10 values. Prior sensitivity shows posterior mean varies 2.6× (0.34→0.89). 50% CI over-coverage 83%. PPP=0.16-0.25. All γ quantitative conclusions should be marked exploratory. R2 fully agrees."}
  action_items:
    - {round: 4, action: "Report Bonferroni and BH corrected results", assigned_to: "paper_agent", status: "done"}
    - {round: 5, action: "Add 'uncorrected for multiplicity' caveat", assigned_to: "paper_agent", status: "done"}
    - {round: 6, action: "Switch main text domain γ to J=16 results", assigned_to: "paper_agent", status: "done"}
    - {round: 10, action: "Resolve P(γ<0) numerical inconsistency between §5.7 (99.7%) and Appendix K Table 10 (98.48%); report P(γ<0) range not single value; downgrade Bonferroni significance claim to 'approaching'; mark all γ conclusions as exploratory in main text", assigned_to: "paper_agent", status: "open"}

- id: "R3-N3"
  summary: "ARC PPP < 0.05 across all J configurations — IRT results unreliable"
  category: method
  severity: warning
  status: in_progress
  first_raised_round: 3
  last_seen_round: 10
  mentions:
    - {round: 3, reviewers: "R1", note: "Within-family J=13 ARC PPP=0.003 not reported."}
    - {round: 4, reviewers: "R1,R2", note: "ARC PPP < 0.05 at all J."}
    - {round: 5, reviewers: "R1,R2", note: "Table 3 now has PPP=0.003. Move ARC IRT to Appendix."}
    - {round: 6, reviewers: "R1,R2", note: "ARC IRT moved to Appendix."}
    - {round: 9, reviewers: "R2", note: "R2 re-raises: ARC PPP=0.003 should be discussed in main text."}
    - {round: 10, reviewers: "R1,R2", note: "R2-W1 re-raises ARC PPP. R1 corrects: PPP=0.003 IS in main text §5.5. R1-W3 adds: MMLU PPP=0.16-0.25 only in Appendix K, not in main text—this is the bigger gap. Both agree MMLU PPP should be reported in main text."}
  action_items:
    - {round: 9, action: "Add brief discussion of ARC PPP=0.003 implications in main text", assigned_to: "paper_agent", status: "done"}
    - {round: 10, action: "Report MMLU PPP=0.16-0.25 in main text §5.5 with brief discussion of model fit limitations", assigned_to: "paper_agent", status: "open"}

